            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Urdu for to put right, then the Urdu for to polish a skill."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: بدعنوانی",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بدعنوانی — badunvānī — \"corruption\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "حکومت بدعنوانی کے خلاف ہے۔ hukūmat badunvānī ke khilāf hai. The government is against corruption."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بدعنوانی (badunvānī) is built from Persian bad, \"bad\", and unvān, \"a heading; a manner\", which is usually traced, through Persian, to Arabic ʿunwān, with the noun ending -ī. Urdu uses it for corruption, bad conduct in office, a sense our sources do not trace."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
